{
 "name": "wheg",
 "description": "Synchronous-tripod 'wheg' stair climber: four tread-sprocket hubs each carry three one-sided 1x11/1x13 liftarm spokes (tips 75.6 mm, 1.3x the 57.6 mm riser) so a spoke always comes down onto the next tread and vaults the hub up instead of relying on friction; left/right spokes in phase (no alternating roll/yaw), 152 mm wheelbase ~ the 148 mm nosing pitch so both axles climb in step at the stair slope; two L motors 1:15 (8-24, 8-40); battery and receiver on a raised deck ahead of the front axle so the light rear axle keeps up; free-turning decoy wheels on two front spokes set the spawn height; timed brake on the top tread.",
